      "source_url": "https://thaqalayn.net/hadith/34/1/47/3",
      "text": [
        " اَلرَّجُلِ يُعْتِقُ غُلاَمَهُ أَوْ جَارِيَتَهُ عَنْ دُبُرٍ مِنْهُ ثُمَّ يَحْتَاجُ إِلَى ثَمَنِهِ أَ يَبِيعُهُ قَالَ \"لاَ إِلاَّ أَنْ يَشْتَرِطَ عَلَى اَلَّذِي يَبِيعُهُ إِيَّاهُ أَنْ يُعْتِقَهُ عِنْدَ مَوْتِهِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.3458 - It is narrated by al-Ala', from Muhammad ibn Muslim, from one of the Imams (as), peace be upon them, regarding a man who frees his male or female slave as a mudabbar (to be freed after his death) and then becomes in need of the slave's price.\nImam (as) said: \"No, he may not sell the slave-unless he stipulates to the buyer that the slave must be freed at the time of his death.\""
        ]
      }
    },
